        "app_persistence_after_restart"
      ],
      "findings": "Round 3: first long-press flags a cell (counter 010->009, flag emoji rendered). All subsequent long-presses (unflag same cell, flag different cell) produce no visible change; later the platform focus-check found the app unresponsive and restarted it. Root cause identified in code review of the reproduction source: UI invalidation relied on a UiState.version counter that is written but never read by any composable, so composition renders stale frames after mutations - gestures do mutate the model and persist, but the screen never recomposes. Visual updates observed earlier coincided with process restarts re-composing from restored state. Fix planned: back the game model with Compose snapshot state (mutableStateOf/SnapshotStateHashSet) so HUD, board and dialogs recompose naturally, and replace manual gesture loops with detectTapGestures.",
