        "licenses_page",
        "licenses_back_navigation"
      ],
      "findings": [
        "Core gameplay verified on the reproduced APK: tap reveals with colored numbers and flood fill; timer starts on first reveal and stops on game over; long-press flags, repeated long-press unflags, flagging a different cell decrements the counter further (010->009->010->009 sequence observed live).",
        "Loss flow verified: tapping a mine explodes the cell, face changes to skull, timer freezes, and the end dialog appears and dismisses on outside tap.",
        "Win flow verified deterministically via Custom 1x1/0: dialog text 'You Win!' / 'Congratulations, you found all the mines in 0 seconds' with Play Again; face shows sunglasses; Play Again starts a new game.",
        "Difficulty switching verified by pixel measurement: Medium renders a 12-column board with counter 040, Hard renders a 14-row board with counter 099; Custom pill displays the configured mine count.",
        "Custom dialog verified: opens from the Custom pill, Width/Height/Mines steppers decrement (150 excess decrements converge to 1/1/0, gates behave), Start game launches the configured board.",
        "Persistence verified: restart_app restores the exact board state (flags, revealed cells, loss state).",
        "Licenses screen opens from the bottom button and system back returns to the game.",
        "Known deviation: the HUD (counter/face/timer) renders without status-bar insets, so it sits under the system status bar; the face button is therefore mostly covered by the status bar touch region and could not be tapped during review (face reset not re-verified in this round). The original app kept the HUD below the status bar. The board also renders flush to the left screen edge (rightmost column slightly clipped on Easy/Hard) instead of the original's centered margins.",
        "One long-press on a closed unflagged cell produced no visible change once mid-game (not reproducible; other long-presses before and after worked). The review emulator also defers frame redraws while idle, which produced stale screenshots between inputs and complicated verification."
      ],
